    "updated_at": "2022-02-08T16:15:20Z",
    "body": "The latest report (https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/issues/3550) suggests that it's been fixed since 3.2.0 (which was released last March). Unfortunately, that does mean that users who rely on distro-packaged versions of the shell will rely on that behavior for some time to come, so if we find that we don't need it for the current fish-latest, I suggest one of two behaviors:\r\n\r\n- Removing the sequence in right-prompt.\r\n- Special-casing on fish version (could be passed from the command line?) to determine if we should draw the character).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
